{"id":"b81162fb77604f8d881c6185390e37fb","model":"gpt-oss-120b","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"answer\": \"Margaret Thatcher\",\n  \"citations\": [\n    [\"United Kingdom local elections, 1980\", 1],\n    [\"Conservative Party (UK) leadership election, 1997\", 1]\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to answer: \"What United Kingdom Prime Minister was succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party?\" The question is ambiguous. Likely asking: Which UK Prime Minister was succeeded (i.e., replaced) in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party. In the 1990s, the Conservative Party leader was John Major (became leader in 1990 after Margaret Thatcher). He succeeded Margaret Thatcher as Prime Minister in 1990. So the Prime Minister succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party (John Major) was Margaret Thatcher. The question: \"What United Kingdom Prime Minister was succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party?\" The leader of the Conservative Party in the 1990s (John Major) succeeded Margaret Thatcher as PM in 1990. So answer: Margaret Thatcher.\n\nWe need citations. Evidence: In the provided evidence, we have \"These were the first annual local elections for the new Conservative Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher.\" That's about 1980. Also we have Federation of Conservative Students mention \"Maggie's Militant Tendency\" referencing Margaret Thatcher. But we need citation that John Major succeeded Margaret Thatcher. Not present directly. However we have evidence: \"The 1997 Conservative Party leadership election was triggered ... when John Major resigned on 2 May 1997, following his party's defeat at the 1997 general election, which ended 18 years of Conservative Government of the United Kingdom.\" That indicates John Major was leader before 1997, but not directly that he succeeded Thatcher. We need a citation that Margaret Thatcher was Prime Minister before John Major. The evidence includes \"These were the first annual local elections for the new Conservative Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher.\" That shows she was PM. Also \"In its final years it became known colloquially as 'Maggie's Militant Tendency', in reference to then Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher\". That also shows she was PM. But we need that John Major succeeded her. Not directly in evidence. However we have \"Major had been Conservative leader and Prime Minister since November 1990.\" That indicates John Major became PM in November 1990, succeeding Thatcher. So we can cite that line: \"Major had been Conservative leader and Prime Minister since November 1990.\" That's from \"Conservative Party (UK) leadership election, 1997\". Actually that line is in that doc. So we can use that as evidence that John Major became PM in 1990, implying he succeeded Thatcher. But we need to answer which PM was succeeded. So answer: Margaret Thatcher. Cite evidence that she was PM and that Major succeeded her. Use two citations: one showing Thatcher was PM (e.g., \"new Conservative Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher\") and one showing Major became PM in November 1990 (implying succession). Provide JSON.\n\n"},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1718,"completion_tokens":652,"total_tokens":2370,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791963238,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}